# Third-party notices

Flezha's binary distributions — the controller container image (`flz_nif.so`
and the `flz` CLI) and the Java SDK jar with the `libflz_core_ffi` native
libraries it bundles — contain the third-party components listed here. Their
license texts and notices are reproduced as those licenses require. Flezha's
own licenses are in `LICENSE` and `LICENSES/`; `REUSE.toml` in the source
repository says which license covers which path.

This file is generated by `cargo about` from `rel/third_party/about.hbs` (run
by `scripts/build-native.sh`); CI fails when it is stale. The Java section is
maintained by hand against the versions pinned in `sdk/java/pom.xml`.

## Java SDK jar — shaded Java dependencies

| Artifact | Version | License |
|---|---|---|
| `com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-core`, `jackson-databind`, `jackson-annotations` | 2.17.2 | Apache-2.0 |
| `com.esotericsoftware:kryo` | 5.6.0 | BSD-3-Clause |
| `com.esotericsoftware:reflectasm` | 1.11.9 | BSD-3-Clause |
| `com.esotericsoftware:minlog` | 1.3.1 | BSD-3-Clause |
| `org.objenesis:objenesis` | 3.3 | Apache-2.0 |
| `com.google.code.findbugs:jsr305` | 3.0.2 | Apache-2.0 (per its POM) |

The Apache License 2.0 text is `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt` in the repository and
`META-INF/LICENSE` in the jar. `jackson-core` bundles FastDoubleParser; its
`META-INF/FastDoubleParser-LICENSE`, `META-INF/FastDoubleParser-NOTICE` and
`META-INF/thirdparty-LICENSE` are carried in the jar unchanged.

